        "path": "_m/g/f/j/2/massacre-of-monzievaird-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Graveyard and Mausoleum at Ochtertyre NN8523 4586044 3c7ab12d.jpg",
        "caption": "Graveyard and Mausoleum at Ochtertyre, near to Hosh, Perth And Kinross, Great Britain. The Mausoleum for the Ochtertyre family was built in 1809 on the site of the old Monzievaird parish church. Nothing of that church remains. It was burned by the Drummonds in 1511, as a retaliation for cattle stealing by the Murrays. The Murrays sought refuge in the church and 120-160 were burned when it caught fire.",
        "alt": "Graveyard and Mausoleum at Ochtertyre, near to Hosh, Perth And Kinross, Great Britain. The Mausoleum for the Ochtertyre family was built in 1809 on the site of the old Monzievaird parish church. Nothing of that church remains. It was burned by the Drummonds in 1511, as a retaliation for cattle stealing by the Murrays. The Murrays sought refuge in the church and 120-160 were burned when it caught fire.",
